    "output": "🔴 Absolutely contraindicated combination. Ketoconazole inhibits both CYP3A4 and P-glycoprotein — Rivaroxaban's sole elimination pathways — increasing anticoagulant exposure by ~160%. Co-administration of Naproxen further multiplies major bleeding risk through platelet inhibition and GI injury in an elderly patient.\n\nConfidence: ✅ HIGH\n\nRecommendation: Discontinue Ketoconazole immediately and substitute with a topical antifungal if cutaneous, or Fluconazole at the lowest effective dose with close INR-equivalent monitoring if systemic therapy is required (note Fluconazole also raises Rivaroxaban levels, but less severely). Discontinue Naproxen and switch to acetaminophen for pain. Review Rivaroxaban indication and consider temporary bridging only if the fungal infection absolutely requires systemic azole therapy, with hematology consultation. Monitor for signs of occult bleeding."
