sphonates are not hepatically metabolized; they are incorporated into bone and excreted renally. The Omeprazole concern relates to GI safety, calcium absorption, and the acid-suppression context — not Alendronate metabolism).\n\n▶ Selected: Interpretation A\n<|tool_call>verify_claim<|\"|>Calcium supplements and Omeprazole impair Alendronate bioavailability, and acid suppression reduces Calcium Carbonate absorption<|\"|>",
