m Tamoxifen, impairing adjuvant breast cancer treatment efficacy<|\"|>",
    "output": "🔴 Bupropion is a strong CYP2D6 inhibitor that significantly reduces conversion of Tamoxifen to its active anticancer metabolite Endoxifen, potentially compromising the efficacy of adjuvant breast cancer therapy.\n\nConfidence: ✅ HIGH\n\nRecommendation: Switch Bupropion to a CYP2D6-sparing antidepressant. Options with minimal CYP2D6 inhibitory activity include: Venlafaxine (also beneficial for cancer-related hot flashes), Escitalopram, Citalopram, Mirtazapine, or Desvenlafaxine. Avoid Fluoxetine (strong CYP2D6 inhibitor) and Duloxetine (moderate CYP2D6 inhibitor). Obtain CYP2D6 pharmacogenomic testing if not already done — if the patient is a native poor metabolizer, Tamoxifen efficacy is already compromised and Aromatase Inhibitor therapy should be considered if she is postmenopausal. Coordinate with medical oncology before any changes."
