ical problem is the central anticholinergic syndrome from Oxybutynin directly impairing the cognitive benefit of the cholinesterase inhibitor).\n\n▶ Selected: Interpretation A\n<|tool_call>verify_claim<|\"|>Oxybutynin's central anticholinergic activity directly antagonizes Donepezil and worsens cognitive impairment in Alzheimer's disease<|\"|>",
