sorption response to thiazide-induced sodium depletion is the dominant effect, causing net Lithium retention, not increased excretion).\n\n▶ Selected: Interpretation A\n<|tool_call>verify_claim<|\"|>Thiazide diuretics reduce renal sodium and cause compensatory Lithium reabsorption, raising serum Lithium levels by 25–50%<|\"|>",
