hibits Cholestyramine's lipid-lowering efficacy. (Leflunomide does not bind bile acids or affect Cholestyramine's mechanism; the interaction is unidirectional — Cholestyramine reduces Leflunomide efficacy, not vice versa).\n\n▶ Selected: Interpretation A\n<|tool_call>verify_claim<|\"|>Cholestyramine interrupts teriflunomide enterohepatic recirculation and rapidly eliminates active Leflunomide metabolite, abolishing RA disease control<|\"|>",
