nhibits Imatinib metabolism causing serious toxicity. (While Omeprazole inhibits CYP2C19, Imatinib's primary metabolism is CYP3A4; the CYP2C19 inhibition effect on Imatinib is minor and does not cause clinically significant toxicity — the dominant concern is the modest absorption reduction).\n\n▶ Selected: Interpretation A\n<|tool_call>verify_claim<|\"|>Omeprazole raises gastric pH and modestly reduces Imatinib bioavailability by approximately 11% which may be clinically relevant in patients not achieving molecular response targets<|\"|>",
