 risk than typicals; the absolute risk is much lower than historical Haloperidol + Lithium cases.\n\n[Discarded Paths]\n✗ Discarded: Olanzapine reduces Lithium levels through enzyme induction. (Olanzapine does not significantly induce CYP enzymes; Lithium is not CYP-metabolized; there is no relevant pharmacokinetic interaction between these agents — the concerns are pharmacodynamic).\n\n▶ Selected: Interpretation A\n<|tool_call>verify_claim<|\"|>Olanzapine and Lithium combination requires metabolic monitoring, ECG baseline, and NMS vigilance despite guideline-supported clinical use<|\"|>",
